Rāma sends Lakṣmaṇa to Gōdāvarī for Sītā --- Lakṣmaṇa searches banks and hears no answer --- Rāma questions Gōdāvarī but fearful river stays silent --- Rāma grieves what to tell Janaka and mother --- Rāma recognizes fallen flowers given to Vaidēhī --- Rāma threatens mountain and river with destruction --- Rāma finds Rākṣasa footprints scattered ornaments and blood --- Rāma infers dreadful fight between two Rākṣasas --- Rāma sees broken bow armor parasol asses chariot and arrows --- Rāma vows to empty worlds of demons and gods